      "body": "### Purpose\r\n_get_rht_signs builds the INT4 Randomized Hadamard Transform sign vector on the CPU and copies it to the GPU on first use. Warmup doesn't run the INT4 KV-cache write path, so with enforce_eager that first use lands inside execute_model, and VLLM_GPU_SYNC_CHECK=error kills the engine:\r\n\r\n_get_rht_signs (int4_per_token_head.py:1142)\r\n```\r\nRuntimeError: GPU<->CPU sync detected - avoid it or wrap with gpu_sync_allowed()\r\nSeen in amd-ci build [#14868](https://buildkite.com/vllm/amd-ci/builds/14868).\r\n\r\n```\r\nThe copy runs once per sign vector (it is cached), so this wraps it in gpu_sync_allowed(). Copy behavior and sign values are unchanged.\r\n\r\n### Test Plan\r\nIn the amd-ci image on MI300X, with VLLM_GPU_SYNC_CHECK=error:\r\n\r\npytest tests/models/quantization/test_per_token_kv_cache.py -k int4_per_token_head\r\npytest tests/quantization/test_per_token_kv_cache.py -k int4\r\n\r\n### Test Result\r\nBefore: the end-to-end int4 test fails with GPU<->CPU sync detected.\r\nAfter: the end-to-end int4 test passes (2 out of 2 runs), and the kernel unit tests pass (26 passed).",
